      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, I can help with that! \"Escrow\" refers to a third-party service that holds funds on behalf of the buyer and seller during the house buying process. By sending money to an escrow account, both parties agree to a fair transaction. The escrow service ensures funds are securely held until all conditions are met, protecting both you and the seller, such as ensuring the house inspection is satisfactory and all necessary documents are signed before releasing the money. This system helps prevent potential fraud and complications that could arise if funds were exchanged directly between buyer and seller.",
